From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:03:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] m2ts_filter: the PIDs it starts with in their order,
 subtitles before menus

_pid_in_list() looks for a PID in a list that it takes to be in
ascending order, and stops at the first larger PID. m2ts_filter_init()
put the menu streams (IG, from 0x1400) before the subtitle streams
(PG, from 0x1200): in a play item with both, a subtitle PID was never
found in the list to wipe, and the subtitles of the clip before the IN
time and after the OUT time came through as if they were of the play
item. The subtitle PIDs now come first.

The order is the one CroqueMr's patch gives them (libreelec-x86-DV,
0002-navigation-read-boundary).
---
 src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c b/src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c
index bad02e2..9273f38 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c
@@ -90,12 +90,13 @@ M2TS_FILTER *m2ts_filter_init(int64_t in_pts, int64_t out_pts,
         for (ii = 0; ii < num_audio; ii++) {
             pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_AUDIO_FIRST + ii;
         }
-        for (ii = 0; ii < num_ig; ii++) {
-            pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_IG_FIRST + ii;
-        }
+        /* in ascending order, as _pid_in_list() takes them: subtitles (PG) before menus (IG) */
         for (ii = 0; ii < num_pg; ii++) {
             pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_PG_FIRST + ii;
         }
+        for (ii = 0; ii < num_ig; ii++) {
+            pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_IG_FIRST + ii;
+        }
     }
 
     return p;
